hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1615","Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, who narrated to us Jarir and Waki', and the wording of this narration is from Jarir, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rode a horse in Medina, and it threw him against the base of a palm tree, dislocating his foot. We went to visit him, and found him in an upper chamber (mashrabah) belonging to Aisha (RA), glorifying Allah while seated. We stood behind him, and he gestured to us to sit, so we sat. When he finished the prayer, he said: \When the Imam prays while seated"," you pray while seated; when the Imam prays while standing"," you pray while standing"," and do not act as the people of Persia act with their nobles.\"""""
